  "featureGroup": false,
  "description": "The \u0027dss_webapps_cached\u0027 dataset provides a comprehensive overview of web applications, capturing essential metadata and operational status. Each entry in the dataset represents a unique web application, identified by a \u0027webapp_id\u0027, and includes descriptive information such as the \u0027webapp_name\u0027 and \u0027webapp_type\u0027. The dataset is particularly useful for managing and monitoring web applications, as it includes details about the associated project (\u0027projectKey\u0027), the creator and last modifier (\u0027created_by_user\u0027, \u0027last_modified_user\u0027), and timestamps for creation and last modification (\u0027created_timestamp\u0027, \u0027last_modified_timestamp\u0027). Additionally, it provides operational status indicators such as \u0027backend_running\u0027 and \u0027is_code_webapp\u0027, which inform whether the backend is active and if the application is code-based, respectively. The \u0027tags\u0027 column allows for categorization through JSON arrays, and the \u0027url\u0027 column provides direct access links to the applications. This dataset is valuable for developers, project managers, and IT administrators who need to track application status, manage user access, and ensure efficient project organization.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of cached web applications with metadata and status information.",
